[00:13.47]Somewhere a window is glowing tonight,
[00:18.02]Somebody's walking beneath the same light,
[00:22.73]Somebody's name is still warm in the air,
[00:27.13]Though nobody living remembers it there.
[00:31.60]There was a room with a red-painted door,
[00:33.93]Young hands were counting the minutes once more,
[00:36.34]Smoke found the ceiling, the ceiling found flame,
[00:38.56]Morning came asking for somebody's name.
[00:40.97]A photograph waits in a drawer out of sight,
[00:43.18]Faces still smiling like everything's right,
[00:45.50]Years keep on running, the numbers grow old,
[00:47.75]But some little stories were never retold.
[00:50.15]And the city keeps moving,
[00:51.21]The river keeps proving
[00:52.29]That everything changes its shape in the rain,
[00:54.36]But somewhere a heartbeat
[00:55.77]Still walks through the street
[00:56.76]Like memory refusing to fade.
[00:59.10]So turn up the light, let it shine through the night,
[01:01.34]Let it dance on the walls where they vanished from sight,
[01:03.73]We carry the spark, we carry the scars,
[01:06.01]We carry the names that were lost in the stars.
[01:08.61]Turn up the light, let tomorrow arrive,
[01:10.45]For the ones who went quiet before they could thrive,
[01:12.87]If history sleeps, let the melody start,
[01:15.14]Some stories disappear, but they stay in the heart.
[01:18.65]Oh-oh, keep the light alive,
[01:20.71]Oh-oh, let the lost survive,
[01:22.98]Not in the numbers, not in the stone,
[01:25.36]But in every life that refuses to go cold.
[01:31.23]There was a mind that could measure the sky,
[01:33.88]A different kind of fire that they couldn't deny,
[01:36.19]They asked it to bend, they asked it to hide,
[01:38.42]And called something broken that burned from inside.
[01:40.80]There was a girl with a page in her hand,
[01:42.83]Writing a world that was harder to understand,
[01:45.24]Outside were the footsteps, inside was a voice,
[01:47.45]A little bit of hope making silence a choice.
[01:50.18]Then somewhere the ground turned the night into day,
[01:51.98]Walls lost their meaning, the streets lost their way,
[01:54.28]A thousand small lives became one silent sound,
[01:56.67]And morning found stories beneath the ground.
[01:59.09]Still the world keeps moving,
[02:00.05]The old clocks keep proving
[02:01.05]That time doesn't stop for a name or a face,
[02:03.55]But somewhere the echoes
[02:04.83]Slip through the shadows
[02:06.06]And quietly ask us to remember the place.
[02:08.38]So turn up the light, let it shine through the night,
[02:10.60]Let it dance on the walls where they vanished from sight,
[02:12.15]We carry the spark, we carry the scars,
[02:14.25]We carry the names that were lost in the stars.
[02:16.64]Turn up the light, let tomorrow arrive,
[02:18.59]For the ones who went quiet before they could thrive,
[02:21.10]If history sleeps, let the melody start,
[02:23.57]Some stories disappear, but they stay in the heart.
[02:28.13]No monument knows every face,
[02:31.66]No book can remember every place,
[02:35.59]No number can tell you the weight of a name,
[02:37.19]No clock can return what the morning reclaimed.
[02:39.55]So when you see a door,
[02:40.63]Think of what it kept.
[02:41.91]When you hear a voice,
[02:42.97]Think of what's left.
[02:45.57]When the ground feels still,
[02:50.32]When the room feels bare,
[02:53.69]There may be someone
[02:56.34]Who was once standing there.
[03:01.61]And we don't need to know every name,
[03:04.02]To know that their lives were never just a frame,
[03:06.18]We don't need to turn every wound into blame,
[03:08.36]We just keep the light from going out the same.
